Included in every edition
-------------------------

International Personality Item Pool (IPIP): Mini-IPIP, IPIP-NEO-120, IPIP
Honesty-Humility facets and revised IPIP-VIA scales.
  Items from the International Personality Item Pool (https://ipip.ori.org/), placed
  in the public domain. The Honesty-Humility and VIA scales are IPIP proxies, not the
  proprietary HEXACO-PI-R or VIA Inventory of Strengths.
  - Donnellan, M. B., Oswald, F. L., Baird, B. M., & Lucas, R. E. (2006). The Mini-IPIP
    scales: Tiny-yet-effective measures of the Big Five factors of personality.
    Psychological Assessment, 18, 192-203.
  - Johnson, J. A. (2014). Measuring thirty facets of the Five Factor Model with a
    120-item public domain inventory: Development of the IPIP-NEO-120. Journal of
    Research in Personality, 51, 78-89.
  - Goldberg, L. R. (1999). A broad-bandwidth, public domain, personality inventory
    measuring the lower-level facets of several five-factor models. In I. Mervielde et
    al. (Eds.), Personality Psychology in Europe, Vol. 7 (pp. 7-28). Tilburg University
    Press.
  - Peterson, C., & Seligman, M. E. P. (2004). Character strengths and virtues: A
    handbook and classification. Oxford University Press.
  Ukrainian versions are Persona Forge project translations and have not been
  psychometrically validated.

Copenhagen Burnout Inventory, work-related burnout scale (English).
  Copenhagen Burnout Inventory, National Research Centre for the Working Environment
  (NFA), Denmark. Source: Borritz M et al., Scand J Public Health 2006; 34: 49-58.
  Used under NFA's free-use grant for commercial and noncommercial use with citation:
  https://nfa.dk/vaerktoejer/spoergeskemaer/spoergeskema-til-maaling-af-udbraendthed-cbi/copenhagen-burnout-inventory-cbi

Private edition only
--------------------

The public edition leaves out the following content until the rights holders
confirm the uses listed in data/permissions.json. The private repository keeps it
for personal use under the terms recorded in each instrument file.

- General Self-Efficacy Scale by Ralf Schwarzer and Matthias Jerusalem (1995).
- NCS-6 items from Lins de Holanda Coelho, Hanel and Wolf (2020), CC BY 4.0, based on
  the Need for Cognition Scale by Cacioppo, Petty and Kao (1984).
- O*NET Interest Profiler Short Form. Includes information from the O*NET Career
  Exploration Tools by the U.S. Department of Labor, Employment and Training
  Administration (USDOL/ETA), used under the CC BY-ND 4.0 license. O*NET is a
  trademark of USDOL/ETA.
- Persona Forge Ukrainian translations of NCS-6 and the Copenhagen Burnout Inventory.
